message: "If you use this book in research, teaching, or technical work, please cite the version you used."
title: "Mastering Blockchain Scalability"
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: "Han"
    given-names: "Neil"
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: 2026-09-02
url: "https://neilydhan.github.io/Blockchain-Scalability-Book/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/neilydhan/Blockchain-Scalability-Book"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  A mechanism-first guide to blockchain scalability as a resource, systems,
  security, and recovery problem. The book covers Layer 1, Layer 2, rollups,
  modular data availability, parallel execution, consensus, threat modeling,
  and benchmark evaluation through end-to-end paths and worked calculations.
keywords:
  - blockchain scalability
  - distributed systems
  - layer 2
  - rollups
  - data availability
  - parallel execution
  - consensus
  - blockchain benchmarking
